j413-speakers.json is a copy of /usr/share/asahi-audio/j413/graph.json
(asahi-audio 4.1) with one change: woofer_lim is retuned into a brickwall
(threshold al 1.0 -> 0.56, about -5 dB, knee 0.5 -> 0.3; ratio cr 15 -> 100).

Why: stock settings let bass-heavy content overshoot the woofer outputs to
+3.9 dB over full scale at 100% volume (11.6% of samples clamped by the DAC),
which is audible clipping on the built-in speakers. Measured 2026-09-01 by
recording the DSP-out stream while playing a bass-heavy test signal.

Adding an LSP limiter_stereo node instead crashes WirePlumber's LV2 loader
(core dump, no worker-feature support), so the existing compressor is retuned.

Wired in by ~/.config/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/99-j413-mic-mono.conf.
After an asahi-audio update, diff against the packaged graph.json and re-apply.
